And that's the final whistle!

36
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,377
There you have it, folks.

37
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:05,160
The groggy ring match is officially over.

38
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:16,417
It's the end of an era.

39
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:19,157
The groggy monsters have
finally been dethroned.

40
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,337
As the kings of the ring.

41
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:22,897
Our new champions and
winners of the second round.

42
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:26,820
are Zoro and Sanji of
the Skullhut Pirates!

43
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:33,837
What'd you think would happen?

44
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:36,137
Like our guys would never lose to you!

45
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:37,220
Hey, Nami!

46
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:38,800
Hey, Robin!

47
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,200
Was I great?

48
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:41,777
Huh, was I?

49
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:43,520
You were just wonderful.

50
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,177
You're nothing but a jerk!

51
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:46,731
Don't scare me like that!

52
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:48,200
Hey, hey, stop.

53
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:51,017
I'm so glad you followed
my plan after all!

54
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:54,100
You really think you had
something to do with this?

55
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:55,190
Now,

56
00:03:55,273 --> 00:03:57,797
as I'm sure you all know,
at the end of our fight,

57
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:01,577
our winners, the Straw Hat Pirates,
can claim their hard-earned prize!

58
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:05,697
Will they take a member of Foxy's crew,
or will they take his Jolly Roger?

59
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:08,977
Either way, it's up to their
captain and their captain alone!

60
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:10,500
Now, drumroll, please!

61
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:17,640
Well, the choice is obvious, isn't it?

62
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:20,484
You mean he's going to pick me?

63
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:21,540
I get it.

64
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:22,977
They want me, don't they?

65
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:25,660
They've wanted me this
whole time. My heart.

66
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:29,260
My heart isn't ready to
say farewell yet. Oh, no.

67
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,894
He's looking this way.

68
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,120
He's gonna take me.

69
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:33,120
I know it.

70
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,660
I bet it'll be me.

71
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:36,100
So long, guys.

72
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,800
I don't want to go.

73
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:42,517
I'll put a smile on my face for my
friends, even if I'm crying on the inside.

74
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,430
Curses.

75
00:04:43,513 --> 00:04:45,184
Why do I have to be so lovable?

76
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:47,260
Come on, Luffy, please.

77
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:50,060
OK, I choose. Hold on a sec.

78
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:53,381
What's up, Nami?

79
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:54,330
Think about it.

80
00:04:54,413 --> 00:04:57,217
Their boss is probably going to
take part in the next round, right?

81
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,217
Sure, we'd all like to get Chopper back.

82
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:02,557
But if we end up losing the next round,
then they'll probably take him right back?

83
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:04,405
and our win would go to waste.

84
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,257
And since his crew will be dumbstruck

85
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:07,637
when they lose their precious boss?

86
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:10,426
we're guaranteed to keep
him for good, get it?

87
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,757
No, say it isn't so.

88
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:17,600
They're really gonna
take our captain away?

89
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,960
But that's the peanut strategy.

90
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,479
You guys are the lowest of the low.

91
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:25,140
Go home, lousy peanuters.

92
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:27,420
Are you afraid to fight us fair?

93
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:30,037
Although there's no rule
against this strategy,

94
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:32,296
it certainly seems a bit underhanded.

95
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:34,517
A little cheating is expected of pirates,

96
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,697
but suddenly taking a cruise
captain away in the middle

97
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:39,037
of a game is no different
than running from a fight.

98
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,000
Shame!

99
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:43,137
Shame on you Straw Hats
and shame on the heartless

100
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:45,197
devil of a woman who
came up with this plan!

101
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:47,920
You're truly a nefarious navigator, Nami!

102
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,040
How dare you talk trash about Nami!

103
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,336
I Outta fillet you!

104
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:55,060
Why are they so mean?

105
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:57,477
Well, even if it doesn't
go against the rules,

106
00:05:57,560 --> 00:06:00,737
it does seem to go against some
of their pirate sensibilities.

107
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:02,349
I'm with Nami on this one!

108
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:03,440
I don't know.

109
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:04,577
I think they're right.

110
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:06,778
Nami, why don't you grow a backbone?

111
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:09,517
You're just making a big
fuss because you lost.

112
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,357
How about you shut up and deal with it?

113
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:12,911
Yes, ma 'am, we're sorry!

114
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:15,757
Underhanded witch, though
she is, the girl is right.

115
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:16,670
Monkey D.

116
00:06:16,753 --> 00:06:18,017
Loopy is the captain of the winning team,

117
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:20,837
so it's up to him to decide
how this battle will unfold.

118
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:25,480
That is to say, he's free to choose
anyone he likes, including Foxy himself.

119
00:06:25,780 --> 00:06:26,610
This is it.

120
00:06:26,693 --> 00:06:28,031
He's picking me for sure.

121
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:31,457
No matter how you slice it, I'm
the only choice that makes sense.

122
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,305
So they're gonna pick me, huh?

123
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:34,837
I knew these guys were cool.

124
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,860
Say, just a quick thought.

125
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:40,377
That plan of yours, although it
would give us a big advantage,

126
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:44,257
you realize it would also make
Foxy a part of our crew. Uh...

127
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:46,720
Yeah, I think I'll pass. Whoa!

128
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:51,717
Now that the Straw Hats are done
emotionally abusing our boss,

129
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:54,137
it's time for them to make their decision.

130
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:57,040
Come on, don't leave us
in suspense any longer.

131
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:01,650
Fine.

132
00:07:01,733 --> 00:07:04,481
In that case, there's
someone I want to take back.

133
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:07,900
Come on, Chopper, get over here!

134
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:10,020
Dad, you better know me that time!

135
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,640
I'll miss you, Choppy!

136
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,560
I was so scared!

137
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:15,380
I'm so happy you won!

138
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:16,900
Are you kidding?

139
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:20,139
Bunch of suckers like that
could never beat my crew.

140
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,390
Oh!

141
00:07:23,473 --> 00:07:26,837
Our sweet captain's heart has been crushed
under the weight of those cruel words!

142
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,997
It's one thing to turn him down, but
did they have to do it like that?

143
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,440
Aw, it's OK.

144
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:33,897
Even if they don't want you, we still do.

145
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:35,568
You're always welcome here.

146
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,860
Do you mean it?

147
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:40,397
Nobody makes fun of our
boss and gets away with it.

148
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,480
Yeah, you'll see.

149
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,737
We'll get him next round.

150
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,797
We won't let you down, boss, I promise.

151
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:45,710
We love you.

152
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:48,280
Don't leave us, you guys.

153
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:49,670
Thank you.

154
00:07:49,753 --> 00:07:51,640
I promise I'll never leave.

155
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:53,700
You're the only crew for me.

156
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,480
Cut the crap, will ya?

157
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:01,677
Just as a fair warning, nobody has ever
been able to beat me in the combat round.

158
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:02,590
Oh, yeah?

159
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:04,916
You think you can beat me in a fight?

160
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:09,080
Maybe so, and maybe not.

161
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:11,620
But this isn't a fight, my boy.

162
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:12,960
It's a game.

163
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,660
One, two, three!

164
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:20,240
Rick finally arrives at the combat round!

165
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:22,877
But before we start, we must
decide on the battlefield!

166
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:25,720
The two competitors spin
this unbiased cannon,

167
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:30,240
and wherever it stops is the
place where they'll do combat!

168
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:35,359
The match hasn't even started yet,
and you guys are cheating already?

169
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:37,397
There you have it!

170
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,037
The battlefield has been set!

171
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,097
And would you look at that!

172
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:43,377
By sheer coincidence, it's
on the deck of the Sexy Foxy!

173
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:45,977
Oh, now you're just rubbing
it in, you little liar!

174
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:49,236
Moving right along, let's
explain the rules of combat!

175
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:52,197
Everything within 50 meters
of where the cannonball

176
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,437
landed is considered
part of the battlefield.

177
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:58,557
In other words, it's a 100-meter-wide circle
measuring from the center of the ship.

178
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:03,117
Weapons and anything else found inside
the designated battlefield are allowed.

179
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,677
However, outside crew members are
strictly forbidden from entering the ship.

180
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:09,077
Knock your opponent out of
bounds and you win the match.

181
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:09,997
Simple as that.

182
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:14,492
Also, as long as you're in the circle
fighting in the air or water is fine.

183
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:17,980
Foxy, Foxy!

184
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:21,157
While we're busy preparing
for the main event,

185
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:24,157
Porch's lovely flower cheerleaders
are performing on the stage.

186
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,397
If that's not your thing,

187
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:28,897
you can also check out a warm-up match
being held on the front of the ship.

188
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:29,977
And as always,

189
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:32,057
our Association of Stulls is selling a

190
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:34,717
limited edition Davey-backed
bite merchandise.

191
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:36,217
So be sure to check that out as well.

192
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:37,337
Nobody wants your junk.

193
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,817
Just start the match already.

194
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:42,135
And here you go, fellas, two
limited edition Foxy Pins.

195
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:44,017
Haven't you seen enough of his young face?

196
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:44,930
We're ready.

197
00:09:45,013 --> 00:09:45,843
Where's your captain at?

198
00:09:45,926 --> 00:09:46,756
He's right there.

199
00:09:46,839 --> 00:09:48,477
Now take him before he
buys something else.

200
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:51,557
Why do I have to pay so much for
your crappy popcorn and cola?

201
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:53,817
If you don't like the price,
how about you don't buy it?

202
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,177
Give me 50 % off.

203
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:56,090
Get out of here.

204
00:09:56,173 --> 00:09:58,800
That cannon means the
preparations are complete.

205
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,157
So if the opening entertainment
could please leave the stage.

206
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,120
Thank you.

207
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:05,496
And now it's time for the main event.

208
00:10:05,780 --> 00:10:09,133
The fighters are in place and
the bell is ready to sound.

209
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:17,273
Grab a seat in the spectator
stands before it's too late.

210
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,360
Now that's odd.

211
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:20,567
It's cloudy all of a sudden.

212
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,417
Today we have a real treat,
ladies and gentlemen.

213
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,820
A Captain vs.

214
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,320
Captain Showdown!

215
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:32,720
First in the left corner, we
have a reigning Davey McChampion!

216
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,417
A man among men who never
turns down a challenge

217
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:39,660
that boasts a legendary
combat record of 920 wins!

218
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:44,660
Our one and only boss,
the Silver Fox Boxer!

219
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:50,200
You listen up, Luffy,
and you listen up good.

220
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,197
You ain't your old self no more.

221
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:56,100
You put that boy to bed, and now
you're gone and woken up a man.

222
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:59,197
Just like that hairstyle's
woken up your wild side.

223
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:02,837
Since the dawn of time, man has
wondered if the champion makes the afro,

224
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:04,537
or the afro makes the champion.

225
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:07,557
But that's a question even
modern science can't answer.

226
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:12,581
Now listen, with that afro on your head,
your fists are weapons of mass destruction.

227
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,837
Strawhead's too scared to come out!

228
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,260
I bet he ran away!

229
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:21,277
And in the right corner, our challenger!

230
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:24,177
Hailing from the east blue
with a tiny crew of only seven!

231
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:29,240
And a massive 100 million fairy bounty,
The rubber wonder they call Strahd,

232
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:32,960
Mountain Davey! Yeah!

233
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:35,350
Yeah!

234
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:41,720
Wow, Luffy is sporting a larger-than-life
afro with a personality to match.

235
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:43,900
Yeah, looking sharp, buddy.

236
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:46,280
That's messed up.

237
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,345
Wow, Luffy's cooler than ever.

238
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,397
I agree.

239
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:54,657
The fighters have entered the battlefield
and look like they're ready to rumble!

240
00:11:54,740 --> 00:11:57,917
Now that Luffy has turned in
his Straw Hat for a mighty afro,

241
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,677
does he have the power to protect the pride
of his crew and unborn children alike?

242
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:05,797
Or will Foxy's undefeated fist strip
him of all his hopes and dreams?

243
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:08,957
Only time will tell as
this fateful final round

244
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:11,580
of the Davy Mac fight
explodes into action!

245
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,740
What's all that stuff?

246
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:19,357
This is the dressing room.

247
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:23,322
You got to wear boxing gloves, but
pretty much anything else goes.

248
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:25,360
This is awesome!

249
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:30,717
This place is more like a costume
shop than a dressing room, you know?

250
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,506
Man, I can't pick a favorite.

251
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:36,251
Do you think it'd be okay if
I just wore all of it at once?

252
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:40,860
Hey, what about this?

253
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,980
Am I cool now?

254
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,430
No.

255
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:46,060
This is it.

256
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:56,665
Hey, Straw Hat, I'm really
diggin' the new lug!

257
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:01,600
I mean, Usa, pull a quick
bait with your left!

258
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,720
Then slap that chin with
a golden uppercut! Yeah!

259
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:08,740
So funky, I can feel that child
lightin' a fire in my soul!

260
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:12,517
You see, this is what happens when
you leave Luffy alone with Usa.

261
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,317
Let me try to show some dignity.

262
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,777
You might be the champ, but
this one's got some bite!

263
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:17,837
He's out of sight!

264
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:19,157
You best get ready to fight!

265
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:21,377
Because this one-two punch
is going to give you up.

266
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:22,754
All right, Corner Man.

267
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:24,737
It's time to take your
sideshow to the sidelines.

268
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:26,337
I was really getting my groove on.

269
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:27,837
You can't make me leave already.

270
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:28,900
Manager out.

271
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,494
Get off with the show.

272
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:35,257
And since I'm not needed here
either, I'll be on my merry way.

273
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:36,928
Let's get this and started.

274
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:41,790
What the?

275
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:43,674
The stands are moving.

276
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,340
Whoa. Cool.

277
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:48,172
I got to get chairs like that on my ship.

278
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:53,948
Now then, Luffy, what do you
say you and I have a little fun?

279
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:57,387
This whole ship is our
playground, after all.

280
00:13:57,580 --> 00:13:59,698
Feel free to go as wild as you like!

281
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:05,088
Don't worry, we have plenty of skilled
shipwrights to clean up after our mess.

282
00:14:08,460 --> 00:14:13,100
Now the opponents face off atop the
fabulous figurehead of the sexy Foxy!

283
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:15,537
Which was chosen by sheer
coincidence, of course!

284
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:19,032
What kind of fearsome flying
fists will be unfurled today?

285
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:20,540
Get him, boss!

286
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:23,469
You can't let that
winning streak stop now!

287
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:25,220
Luffy, don't lose!

288
00:14:25,380 --> 00:14:26,437
That's all that matters!

289
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:28,500
Just watch out for his beam, OK?

290
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:32,397
Excitement fills the stands in the
final seconds before the match.

291
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:34,620
It's plunder or be plundered. Luffy!

292
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:35,940
Go boss!

293
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:40,620
It's the Silver Slow Slow Slugger
versus the Gum-Gum Jatling Gun.

294
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:43,357
This is a one-round
bout with no time limit.

295
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:46,257
As long as they stay in
bounds, Everything goes!

296
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,740
The fighters are ready!

297
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:50,900
And there goes the bell!

298
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,857
Yeah, you! Go on to go!

299
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:55,900
Slow, slow, me!

300
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:05,240
My arm is fast, but my fist is all slow!

301
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:10,312
You don't expect me to be
afraid of a rubber hose, do you?

302
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:11,440
Give me a sec!

303
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:12,910
Come back!

304
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:18,380
Slow, slow, baby!

305
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:21,420
I fooled you!

306
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,260
Slow, slow, baby!

307
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:28,370
That's me!

308
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:33,080
Wow, he's floating.

309
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:35,617
I guess that means he falls slow, too.

310
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,637
I told him to watch out for that.

311
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:39,249
Why won't he listen to me?

312
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:48,517
I know there's no time limit, but come on!

313
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,637
Why don't you spare us both and give up?

314
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:54,440
No way!

315
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:58,100
Nine tails around!

316
00:16:02,340 --> 00:16:03,170
Oh!

317
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:06,177
Our boss on Gleasius' signature
attack right off the bat!

318
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:08,436
Stronghead is helpless to fight back!

319
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:11,380
This is crazy.

320
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:13,220
He's not budging an inch.

321
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:14,560
No, look closely.

322
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:16,782
He's just moving in slow motion.

323
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:29,117
Consider that a preview of what's to come,

324
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:32,697
though, to your credit, it seems like
you can take a punch pretty well.

325
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:35,657
Fortunately, I've got plenty
of other tricks up my sleeve.

326
00:16:35,740 --> 00:16:38,200
Come back here.

327
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:41,180
Well, your 30 seconds are about up.

328
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:46,140
He's falling overboard. No, baby!

329
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:59,057
That slow, slow beam is going to
give me more trouble than I thought.

330
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:01,380
Wow, beams sure are cool, huh?

331
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:05,446
Still, I've got to be more careful
where I stretch my arms now.

332
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:07,976
Where'd that jerk run off to, anyway?

333
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:13,073
I won't let you sneak up on
me with your beam, Splithead!

334
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:16,800
Come on and fight like a man!

335
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:21,025
I understand your frustration,
but don't take it out on the air!

336
00:17:25,340 --> 00:17:27,400
Did he use his beam?

337
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:33,397
Welcome to the sexy boxy, Rubber Boy.

338
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:34,833
That was a dirty trick.

339
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,020
He got me!

340
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:41,476
Just calm down for a second, will ya?

341
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:44,697
Can't you see I'm trying to
show you some hospitality here?

342
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:47,417
Those cannonballs are
moving in slow-mo, too.

343
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:51,180
Well, if you can ride
on one, then so can't I!

344
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:52,561
Be careful, kid!

345
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:55,093
I wouldn't touch that one if I were you!

346
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:57,680
Ah, and that one, too.

347
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:03,117
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

348
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,847
Can't say I didn't warn you!

349
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:15,780
What's his problem anyway?

350
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:19,021
If he keeps this up, he's
gonna sink his own ship.

351
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:21,400
I'll sink you first!

352
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:23,660
Slow, slow, foxy-faced bomb tenor!

353
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:27,770
Creepy!

354
00:18:31,300 --> 00:18:32,740
Huh? Oh, they're pins.

355
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:35,117
They sure are a lot bigger
than the one I bought, though.

356
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,597
Of course we're bigger, stupid.

357
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:38,417
That's because we're bomb-stupid.

358
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:39,440
Wait, what?

359
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:40,800
Did you say bomb?

360
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,000
Why is a bomb talking?

361
00:18:44,100 --> 00:18:45,960
I'm the real thing, that's why!

362
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:50,992
My punches weren't quite doing the trick.

363
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:53,480
So I upgraded my gloves, see?

364
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:57,096
Oh, and fair warning, those
bombs are about to go off.

365
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:03,120
Yeah! Body blue! Body blue!

366
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:04,520
Oh, it's Usopp.

367
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:07,497
Hey, what's going on with
the fight down there?

368
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,320
Uh, I don't have a clue.

369
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:10,880
Are you kidding me?

370
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:28,160
A series of powerful
explosions rocks our ship!

371
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:31,388
Which just so happens
to be the battlefield!

372
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:36,017
The likely cause of some foxy merchandise
that just happens to be explosive!

373
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:39,197
All this cheating just so
happens to be pissing me off.

374
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:41,317
No wonder that jerk's never lost a match.

375
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,840
Loopy, speak to me!

376
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:44,500
Hey, sit down.

377
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:46,717
Using his surroundings to his advantage,

378
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:51,329
our boss slammed Straw Hat head-on with
a strategically placed cannon attack.

379
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:53,500
All I can see is smoke.

380
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:55,879
Was Straw Hat blown to smithereens?

381
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:58,420
That was a close one.

382
00:19:58,600 --> 00:20:00,600
Indeed, Foxy's onslaught was...

383
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:06,060
Shut up! You're annoying!

384
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,520
That's a miracle!

385
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:10,560
Shawhat Luffy is alive!

386
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:13,877
Whoa, he's alive!

387
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:14,842
There's no way!

388
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:19,360
He somehow abated the explosive
attack at point-blank range!

389
00:20:19,540 --> 00:20:20,820
What amazing speed!

390
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:24,689
The 100 million Barry Rubber
Boy is truly a thing of wonder!

391
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:26,157
At the power of the frog!

392
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:27,358
Hurry it up, Luffy!

393
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:42,700
Uh-oh!

394
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,937
It looks like our boss's next
attack is already underway!

395
00:20:46,020 --> 00:20:48,138
What could it be plotting this time?

396
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:56,420
The sneaky foxy lets out an unsettling
laugh from behind a thick screen of smoke.

397
00:20:56,700 --> 00:20:59,437
Meanwhile, Straw Hat stares
cluelessly into the abyss.

398
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:01,260
The suspense is killing me!

399
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:02,911
Where is our boss hiding?

400
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:04,820
Is that him?

401
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:15,640
Oh, how'd you like that? You had enough?

402
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:18,080
You got blown up twice as bad as me!

403
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:20,340
Shut up, I'm fine! See?

404
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:21,790
Look!

405
00:21:21,873 --> 00:21:23,177
You don't look fine at all!

406
00:21:23,260 --> 00:21:25,237
I don't even want you on my crew anymore.

407
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:26,717
I'd rather just crush you.

408
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:27,940
Slow, slow me!

409
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:29,290
Gum, gum!

410
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:35,378
I'm going to break your arm so you
can't hit me with those dumb beads.

411
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,310
Ah!

412
00:21:36,393 --> 00:21:38,199
Does this guy want to fight or not?

413
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:41,070
There you are!

414
00:21:41,220 --> 00:21:42,050
Gotcha!

415
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,030
Huh?

416
00:21:44,113 --> 00:21:45,060
It was just a cutout?

417
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:46,600
Slow, slow beam!

418
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:58,540
Hey, hey, hey! Now what?

419
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:00,940
Which one is the real me?

420
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:03,217
Which direction will the beam come from?

421
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:04,500
How should I know?

422
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:09,365
They all look the same, just a bunch of
split heads with stupid-looking haircuts.

423
00:22:09,860 --> 00:22:12,320
Oh, now a stupid-looking split head?

424
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:15,990
That one!

425
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:23,990
You jerk!

426
00:22:24,200 --> 00:22:26,257
I may be a cheater, but
at least I have a heart!

427
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:28,120
You're in for it now! Look up!

428
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:34,130
Ah!

429
00:22:35,460 --> 00:22:37,180
Damn it! A trap door!

430
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:40,097
That's what you get for keeping
your head in the clouds!

431
00:22:40,180 --> 00:22:43,533
You're the one who told me to
look up in the first place!

432
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:44,880
So I did!

433
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:46,394
Better look down, too!

434
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:50,912
Why is the floor moving?

435
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:56,460
Fuck! It's Loopy!

436
00:22:56,580 --> 00:22:58,297
If he falls in the water, he's done for!

437
00:22:58,380 --> 00:23:00,277
Come on, you can't let
the fight ends this way!

438
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:03,020
You can get rid of me that easy!

439
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:08,200
Close call!

440
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:13,537
It wouldn't be any fun if Boss
knocked him out right off the bat.

441
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:15,091
Hang in there, Straw Hat!

442
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:16,500
After power!

443
00:23:17,460 --> 00:23:20,020
This ship's a pain in
the butt! What gives?

444
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:23,040
Hey, Splithead, where'd you go?

445
00:23:25,260 --> 00:23:26,500
What happened here?

446
00:23:26,980 --> 00:23:30,277
Straw Hat's narrow escape didn't
seem to impress this foxy pin.

447
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:32,713
You might even say it's laughing at him.

448
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:34,300
So there you are.

449
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:36,697
The cabin of the ship
is Foxy's playground.

450
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:38,157
Will Luffy be lured inside?

451
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:39,960
Hold on, Luffy, it's a trap.

452
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:42,613
Whatever you do, do not go in that ship.

453
00:23:45,520 --> 00:23:47,932
I'm going to beat that jerk's brains out.

454
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:51,437
Straw Hat throws caution to the
wind and dashes inside the ship.

455
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:54,537
Unfortunately, that means I can't
give you play-by-play anymore.

456
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:56,457
But I think it's safe to
assume that whatever's

457
00:23:56,540 --> 00:23:58,937
going on in there is completely amazing.

458
00:23:59,020 --> 00:24:00,240
But leave!

459
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,997
It's time to put those
wings to the Tesla bird!

460
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:04,277
So spread them and fly!

461
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:07,177
These seats are bad enough
without you standing in the way.

462
00:24:07,260 --> 00:24:08,840
Cool. A gun deck.

463
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:10,140
It's huge, too.

464
00:24:10,460 --> 00:24:11,857
Too bad Usopp isn't here.

465
00:24:11,940 --> 00:24:12,822
He'd love this.

466
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:14,940
Now, where'd Foxy run off to?

467
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:18,460
Aha! He's over there!

468
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:25,220
All right, good.

469
00:24:25,420 --> 00:24:26,617
He's coming after me.

470
00:24:26,700 --> 00:24:30,112
And now he'll come rushing
through that door like an idiot

471
00:24:31,060 --> 00:24:34,617
But we'll see how chipper our
little rubber boy is Who in my

472
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:38,465
room full of two-foot steel spikes
makes Swiss cheese out of him

473
00:24:39,940 --> 00:24:42,140
Come on, Straw Hat, you know you won

474
00:24:54,500 --> 00:24:58,560
Hey, it's him Wow, wonder
what that room's used for.

475
00:24:58,740 --> 00:25:02,622
What kind of monster fires off
cannons inside someone else's ship?

476
00:25:04,560 --> 00:25:07,140
At least he stopped running away.

477
00:25:12,440 --> 00:25:15,040
You brain die!

478
00:25:17,860 --> 00:25:19,820
I'll show you, just wait.

479
00:25:20,280 --> 00:25:21,360
No way!

480
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:23,860
Come back and fight me!

481
00:25:27,180 --> 00:25:29,827
Doesn't he have any
common decency, honestly?

482
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:33,860
I've had enough foxy-faced transformation.

483
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,880
I got you now!

484
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:40,350
Who's that?

485
00:25:40,433 --> 00:25:42,060
Dear me, are you ill?

486
00:25:42,260 --> 00:25:44,137
Tell me where it hurts and I'll fix it.

487
00:25:44,220 --> 00:25:46,060
Is it your head? Is that it?

488
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:47,617
Are you sick in the head?

489
00:25:47,700 --> 00:25:48,530
Wait a sec.

490
00:25:48,613 --> 00:25:50,357
Did you see someone
else come through here?

491
00:25:50,440 --> 00:25:52,380
Why, no, I didn't see a soul.

492
00:25:52,580 --> 00:25:53,517
But never mind that.

493
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:55,482
You broke something, didn't you?

494
00:25:55,580 --> 00:25:56,462
You had a face?

495
00:25:58,160 --> 00:26:01,300
I could have sworn I saw
him go in there. Hold on.

496
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:03,971
That weird lady, she looked just like him.

497
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:10,080
I get it.

498
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:12,420
Hey, you must be Foxy's sister.

499
00:26:12,520 --> 00:26:13,537
You can't fool me.

500
00:26:13,620 --> 00:26:15,320
It's Hunter Foxy. No!

501
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:22,600
What the heck is this?

502
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:27,940
So that's it!

503
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:30,817
She lied to me so I
wouldn't fight her brother!

504
00:26:30,900 --> 00:26:32,959
Is he even trying to fight anymore?

505
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:35,710
The kitchen!

506
00:26:37,720 --> 00:26:39,537
Slice of the fish, what do you know?

507
00:26:39,620 --> 00:26:41,320
You got some nice carpaccio.

508
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:43,497
Don't forget to cut a tarot.

509
00:26:43,580 --> 00:26:45,360
Do-re-mi-fas-or-a-ti-do.

510
00:26:46,900 --> 00:26:48,020
Ahem. Yes?

511
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:50,557
Have you seen some old
fox dude with his head

512
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:53,640
split in two that looks
really stupid and not cool?

513
